  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "c386da25-df9c-4f9d-ace5-7103a6c389fd",
      "phaseId": "4d4aa26b-6245-4c0f-8bdf-64573a7afbf5",
      "number": 308,
      "shortId": "DV7J8",
      "priority": 2,
      "shortName": "layout-settings-self-describin",
      "title": "Layout settings: self-describing, applied to every widget kind, zero per-property code",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "DEPENDS ON T1 (the layout/visual split). Closes gap 1 of the phase description.\n\nCURRENT STATE\n`realize_flex` (heca/src/chrome/realize.rs:440-459) reads exactly TWO layout properties — `gap` and\n`align` — and only for `Column`/`Row`. Every other layout setting on `Style` is unreachable from a\n`ViewNode`: padding, justify, width, height, direction, margins, min/max sizes, flex_grow,\nflex_shrink, the spacing tokens, hidden, grid_cell.\n\nTHE PRECEDENT TO FINISH (not invent)\n`realize` already applies two properties generically for EVERY kind, at realize.rs:100-112:\n    let mut realized = realize_kind(node, emit, hints, forms);\n    if let Some(align) = align_prop(node, \"align_self\") { ...base_mut().style.align_self = ... }\n    if let Some(justify) = align_prop(node, \"justify_self\") { ... }\nwith the comment: \"Self-alignment is a property of the node *inside its parent*, so it applies to\nevery kind — read it once here rather than in each arm.\"\nThat is the correct pattern, started and abandoned. This task finishes it.\n\nWHY NOT A HAND-WRITTEN apply_style_props()\nExplicitly rejected by the user 2026-07-25: a function listing each field still needs a new line\nevery time a `Style` field is added. It relocates the drift instead of removing it. The property\nlist must BE A TYPE that a generator reads.\n\nWORK\n- Add serialization to the LAYOUT group produced by T1. `heca-grid-ui` has NO serialization\n  dependency today (Cargo.toml:8-12 — heca-core, heca-theme, floem_reactive, taffy), so this adds\n  one, plus derives on the types the layout group holds: `Length`, `Align`, `Justify`, `Direction`,\n  `Spacing`, `GridCell` (and `WidgetSize` if T1 puts the semantic group here).\n- In `realize`, merge the node's properties into the realized widget's layout settings, replacing\n  the two hand-written blocks at realize.rs:104-111 AND the gap/align reads in realize_flex.\n- Property NAMES must match the field names so the mapping needs no table. Where a field name is a\n  poor public name, rename the field rather than adding a lookup — a lookup is the drift again.\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Untrusted input: `realize` is TOTAL by design (view.rs rustdoc: \"Missing/mistyped props are\n  ignored (the widget keeps its default)\"). A bad value must leave the default in place, never\n  panic and never abort the rest of the merge. Keep this behaviour and test it.\n- Widgets set deliberate non-default layout in their constructors — e.g. `ScrollRegion::new()` sets\n  min_width/min_height to Px(0.0), flex_shrink Some(1.0), pad_spacing_y and gap_spacing\n  (scroll_region.rs:188-214), each with a comment explaining why. The merge must apply ON TOP of\n  the constructed widget, overriding only properties the node actually carries. Never build from a\n  default `Style`, or every ScrollRegion silently stops scrolling.\n- `size` is already read via `size_prop` (realize.rs:493, 946) and cascades to children. Do not\n  double-apply it.\n\nACCEPTANCE\n- Every layout setting is reachable from a `ViewNode` on every kind.\n- realize.rs contains NO list of layout property names.\n- A test proves a new `Style` field is reachable with no change to realize.rs.\n- Totality test: nonsense values are ignored, defaults survive, nothing panics.\n- ScrollRegion's constructor-set layout survives a merge that does not mention those fields.\n- Update BOTH the props-by-kind table in view.rs's rustdoc (view.rs:311-337) and docs/widgets.md.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nDONE 2026-07-25 — commit def0967. User verified in the showcase: no visual change.\n\nWHAT LANDED\n`realize.rs` contains NO layout property name in non-test code (verified by grep). `merge_layout_props`\n(heca/src/chrome/realize.rs, called from `realize`) serializes the CONSTRUCTED widget's\n`style.layout` to a JSON map, overlays only the keys the node carries, and deserializes back.\nThe field list is `Layout`'s own fields — derived, never written down.\n\nTHREE HAND-WRITTEN BLOCKS DELETED (all replaced by the one merge):\n- `align_self` / `justify_self` at the top of `realize` (the original half-finished precedent).\n- `gap` / `align` in `realize_flex`.\n- `align` / `justify_items` in the Grid arm. The pre-existing Grid test passes UNCHANGED — that is\n  the proof the generic path covers what the hand-written reads did.\n\nNEWLY REACHABLE FROM A ViewNode (none worked before): padding, padding_x/y, pad_spacing_x/y,\nmargin + 4 per-side overrides, width, height, min/max width+height, justify, direction, flex_grow,\nflex_shrink, hidden, grid_cell, gap_spacing.\n\nDESIGN DECISIONS\n- `Length` got a hand-written Serialize/Deserialize (heca-grid-ui/src/style.rs) so it reads as an\n  author would write it: bare number = px, \"auto\" = Auto, \"50%\" = Pct(0.5). NOT the derived\n  `{\"px\": 240}` shape. It ROUND-TRIPS, which the merge depends on (it serializes current state\n  first). One impl, no per-field work.\n- Enums travel by NAME in snake_case (\"center\", \"space_between\", \"small\"), consistent with how\n  glyphs and colours already cross. Derived on Direction/Justify/Align/WidgetSize/Spacing/GridCell.\n- `Layout` is `#[serde(default)]` so a partial map deserializes.\n- serde added to heca-grid-ui (version = \"1\", features = [\"derive\"]) — the crate had no\n  serialization dependency before. `Visual` deliberately derives NOTHING; that is the boundary.\n- TOTALITY IS PER-PROPERTY: fast path merges all keys at once; on failure it falls back to applying\n  one key at a time and keeping only those that fit. A misspelled length no longer discards the\n  good props on the same node. Keys that do not name a `Layout` field are skipped by checking\n  against the serialized map (i.e. against the real field list).\n\nSAFETY CHECK WORTH REPEATING FOR LATER TASKS: because previously-ignored props now take effect,\nI grepped for any app-side ViewNode setting a layout prop that had been silently dropped — every\nhit was in test code, so no production tree changed behaviour. Do this check whenever a prop\nbecomes newly live.\n\nTESTS — 5 new in realize.rs's test module, 904 green overall, clippy 0:\n- `layout_properties_never_named_in_realize_still_reach_the_widget` — padding/width/justify/\n  flex_grow/margin on a Column. THE regression guard: it fails the moment someone reintroduces a\n  hand-written property list that omits one.\n- `length_accepts_the_spelling_an_author_would_reach_for`\n- `a_bad_property_never_takes_the_good_ones_with_it`\n- `merging_preserves_layout_the_widget_set_in_its_constructor` (ScrollRegion min sizes +\n  flex_shrink + gap_spacing survive)\n- `a_node_with_no_properties_changes_nothing`\n\nDOCS: view.rs rustdoc gained a \"Layout props — every kind, no list\" section ahead of the\nprops-by-kind table (whose Column/Row row now reads \"layout only — see above\"); docs/widgets.md\nmirrors it with a worked example.\n\nNOTE FOR T4: the same merge mechanism does NOT cover widget-specific settings (placeholder, scroll\naxes) — those are fields on individual widget structs, which is T3's problem.",
