    {
      "id": "6e2a7db7-0092-471a-9db3-ff1fbb685152",
      "phaseId": "4d4aa26b-6245-4c0f-8bdf-64573a7afbf5",
      "number": 312,
      "shortId": "J2LU8",
      "priority": 6,
      "shortName": "expose-the-clickable-row-widge",
      "title": "Expose the clickable Row widget — rename the KIND (decided 2026-07-27)",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "Closes gap 4 of the phase description.\n\n# ✅ DECIDED BY THE USER 2026-07-27 — Option A, plus the symmetry follow-on\n\n**`WidgetKind::Row` → `WidgetKind::HStack`. `WidgetKind::Column` → `WidgetKind::VStack`. The name `Row` is freed for the real interactive widget.**\n\nThe two questions were put to the user with the trade-offs and the counts (the widget: 11 call sites in 3 files; the kind: 7 code sites + ~40 doc mentions). Both answers were the recommended one:\n\n1. **Which `Row` gives up the name → the KIND.** Truest to the library, and nothing outside this repo consumes the vocabulary yet — no WASM plugin exists — so the breakage is internal and only grows if deferred.\n2. **Does `Column` follow → YES, `VStack`.** The pair stays symmetric and both names read as layout, which is the point. Renaming it later would be a second churn through the same files.\n\nThe alternatives are closed: naming the new kind something else (leaves the library's `Row` and the model's `Row` permanently different things) and renaming the library widget (the widget has the better claim to the name). **Do not re-open them.**\n\n# THE COLLISION (verified in code 2026-07-25, still true 2026-07-27)\n\nTwo different things are called Row.\n- `heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/row.rs` — a REAL WIDGET. Its own doc header: \"a **focusable, clickable\n  container** for arbitrary composed content… `Item` is the fixed leading/label/trailing row; `Row`\n  is its open cousin: it provides the same interactive chrome — hover tint, active (selected) state\n  with an `ActiveMarker`, press flash, focus ring, and `on_activate` (mouse + Enter/Space) — but\n  holds **any** children… Use it for rich Dock rows that need to be clicked and selected, where\n  `Item`'s slots aren't enough.\" `on_activate` is at row.rs:96.\n- `WidgetKind::Row` — maps to `Flex::row()` (realize.rs:124). A plain horizontal box. No focus, no\n  hover, no press, no activation.\n\nCONSEQUENCES\n- The interactive Row widget has NO declarative spelling at all. A plugin cannot make a clickable,\n  selectable rich row — the exact thing the widget was built for.\n- docs/chrome-and-ui.md example 2 writes `Row::new().gap(12) … .on_press(intent(\"plugin.docker.select\",\n  {\"id\": …}))` for a clickable table row. That is the WIDGET's behaviour written against the KIND\n  that cannot do it. The published example is wrong in a way no reader could detect.\n- Anyone reading `WidgetKind::Row` in the app and `Row` in the library reasonably assumes they are\n  the same thing. They are not.\n\n# WORK\n\n**1. Rename the two layout kinds.** `Row` → `HStack`, `Column` → `VStack`, everywhere: `WidgetKind` and `ALL` and `ordinal` (view.rs), the `realize` arms (realize.rs:124), every native construction site, the props-by-kind rustdoc table, docs/widgets.md, docs/chrome-and-ui.md, README.md, AGENTS.md. Note `WidgetKind` is `#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]`, so the wire spelling changes from `\"row\"`/`\"column\"` to `\"h_stack\"`/`\"v_stack\"` — check that reads as intended, and consider an explicit `#[serde(rename)]` if `hstack`/`vstack` is wanted instead. **Record which spelling was chosen and why.**\n\n**2. Add `WidgetKind::Row` for the interactive widget** + a `realize` arm mapping it to `heca_grid_ui::Row`.\n\n**3. Wire it as ACTIONABLE.** It needs its `press` event on BOTH a click handler and a KeyHint target, the same way the `Button` arm does (realize.rs:461+ — \"wiring its `press` intent to both a click handler and a hint target… a click emits it, the picker fires it\"). Without the hint target, `prefix+/` cannot reach it.\n\n**4. Selected/active state** — follow `Item`'s arm, which already has the precedent. Do not invent a second spelling for the same idea.\n\n**5. Properties come from the generated surface** (`with_props`), not a hand-written list — the T3 mechanism. Check `Row`'s builders are all `#[prop]`/`#[host_only]` classified; the macro will refuse to compile otherwise.\n\n**6. The coverage fixture** in realize.rs (`sample_node`) needs an arm: `Row` is a container that is also actionable, so give it a child AND a press intent.\n\n# ACCEPTANCE\n- A description can produce a clickable, selectable rich row that behaves exactly like the native one.\n- The rename is applied consistently across code AND every document — no file left saying `WidgetKind::Row` means a flex box.\n- Coverage + `all_lists_every_widget_kind` guards pass.\n- docs/chrome-and-ui.md example 2 becomes correct rather than aspirational.\n- **USER verifies click, keyboard activation, hover and selected state in the showcase** — this is interactive behaviour, so tests alone do not close it (see the `no-unverified-rendering-widget-changes` rule).\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nDONE 2026-07-27 — commit a413730 on branch `feat/action-arg-declaration`. NOT pushed.\n\n## DECISION APPLIED (user, 2026-07-27)\n\nOption A plus the symmetry follow-on: **`WidgetKind::Row` → `HStack`, `WidgetKind::Column` → `VStack`**, and the freed name `Row` went to the real interactive widget. Both answers were the recommended one, taken with the counts on the table (the widget: 11 call sites in 3 files; the kind: 7 code sites + ~40 doc mentions).\n\n**Wire spelling:** `WidgetKind` is `#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]`, so the wire form is `\"h_stack\"` / `\"v_stack\"`. Kept rather than pinned to `\"hstack\"`: the model's own stated rule (docs/chrome-and-ui.md Part I §6) is that enums travel as their name in lower case with underscores, and a hand-written `#[serde(rename)]` would have been an exception to it for cosmetics.\n\n## WHAT SHIPPED\n\n- `heca/src/chrome/view.rs`: the two renames through the enum, `ALL` and `ordinal`; a new `Row` variant at ordinal 2 with rustdoc explaining what it is and what it used to be.\n- `heca/src/chrome/realize.rs`: the `Row` arm. `active` / `nav_selected` / `marker` arrive through the generated surface (`with_props`); the press is wired to a click, to Enter/Space, **and** to a KeyHint target the way the `Button` arm does, so `prefix+/` reaches it. Imported as `Row as GridRow` since `Row` is now also a `WidgetKind`.\n- **With no press intent the row stays inert** — not focusable, no hover. A described row nothing can activate should not look like a control.\n- Coverage fixture: `Row` needs both a child and a press intent, or it reads as \"realized to nothing\".\n\n## TESTS\n\n- `a_described_row_is_clickable_and_keyboard_activatable` — dispatches a real `PointerPressed` and a real `GridKey::Enter` through the realized widget; both fire the same intent with its args; one hint target registered; content held.\n- `a_described_row_without_a_press_intent_is_inert`.\n\n## DOCS\n\ndocs/chrome-and-ui.md's table example was the reason this task existed — it wrote the widget's behaviour (press, selection) against the kind that had none of it, undetectably. It now uses `HStack` for the header and a real clickable `Row` for the body rows, with a note on what changed and when. Also: docs/widgets.md (`Row` gains its declarative half + a \"Row is not HStack\" note), the props-by-kind tables in view.rs and widgets.md, the vocabulary lists in AGENTS.md and docs/widget-architecture.md, and widget-architecture.md's own example.\n\n## ⚠️ VERIFICATION — WHAT WAS AND WAS NOT CHECKED\n\nThe acceptance asked the user to click through the described row in the showcase. **That is impossible and the task should not have promised it:** the showcase lives in `heca-renderer`, which is BELOW `heca` in the crate graph, so it cannot call `realize` at all. The only production caller of `realize` is a modal body, so no described `Row` appears anywhere in the running app.\n\nWhat was verified instead: the interaction test above drives real pointer and key events through the real widget. The **native** `Row` (the showcase PANES cards) is untouched by this task.\n\nThe user was told this plainly rather than the box being ticked. The underlying limitation is recorded on **F003/P017/T009**, which gained this as a second motivation independent of plugins.\n\n## GATE\n\n`cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features` 0 warnings; `cargo test --workspace` green across 20 suites; showcase builds.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
      "checklist": [
        {
          "id": "6e2a7db7-0092-471a-9db3-ff1fbb685152-check-001-blocking-put-options-a-b-c-to-the-user-with-the-trade-offs-do-not-pick-silently",
          "title": "BLOCKING: put options A / B / C to the user with the trade-offs; do not pick silently",
          "checked": false
        },
        {
          "id": "6e2a7db7-0092-471a-9db3-ff1fbb685152-check-002-add-the-kind-realize-arm-mapping-to-the-row-widget",
          "title": "Add the kind + realize arm mapping to the Row widget",
          "checked": false
        },
        {
          "id": "6e2a7db7-0092-471a-9db3-ff1fbb685152-check-003-wire-press-intent-and-a-keyhint-target-follow-the-button-arm-else-prefix-cannot-reach-it",
          "title": "Wire press → intent AND a KeyHint target (follow the Button arm), else prefix+/ cannot reach it",
          "checked": false
        },
        {
          "id": "6e2a7db7-0092-471a-9db3-ff1fbb685152-check-004-handle-selected-active-state-the-way-item-s-arm-already-does",
          "title": "Handle selected/active state the way Item's arm already does",
          "checked": false
